WEBVTT

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:12.400
<b>Special Public Security Fifth Division 
Third Mobile Assault Unit 8</b>

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:07.690
<i>Special Public Security Fifth Division,</i>

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.290
<i>Third Mobile Assault Unit 8.</i>

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.820
<i>AKA Unit 8.</i>

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.070
<i>As you all know,</i>

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.310
<i>they are part of the police's ACTIVE project, 
which allows them to use Willwears.</i>

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.410
<i>They're at the project's cutting edge, 
and they're also the heroes who</i>

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.150
<i>saved Japan from the Logos Incident.</i>

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.180
<i>Picking up where we left off last week,</i>

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.750
<i>I'm here again with Inspector Kuroki, 
the ace of Unit 8!</i>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.700
<i>I'm Kuroki Takeru.</i>

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.470
<i>Thanks for having me.</i>

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.680
<b>Old City Hall, Demolition Site</b>

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.250
What, this is all you've got?

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.190
If you want to date me, get more money!

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.540
Who the hell are you, 
and why are you in a Willwear?

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:53.360
You...

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.030
I have a fun job where you 
can earn more than that.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:56.860
How about it?

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:00.530
Let me see...

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:04.160
The gym, large-scale bathhouses... 
 And I like cream pound cake,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.280
but the one who bought it for me is gone now.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.500
You're a hero, but you have common tastes!

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:13.210
I never thought I'd see the day when 
you'd call me a hero, Komieri-chan.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:17.360
I'm sorry I was always so negative 
when I was a newscaster.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.300
By the way, I hear you're 
going to graduate school?

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.480
<i>Yes. At the last Diet meeting,</i>

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.810
<b>Nagoya City, Hisaya Odori</b>

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>they reviewed the laws, in particular 
with respect to our authority</i>

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:29.030
<i>to independently investigate 
terrorist organizations.</i>

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:33.030
<i>I figured I should dig a little deeper into it.</i>

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.320
<i>And...</i>

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.650
<i>There aren't enough of us</i>

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:40.320
<b>New City Hall: Hachioji City, Tokyo</b>

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.860
<i>to cover the entire country.</i>

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.830
<i>I want to learn from people across the country.</i>

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:45.290
<i>The use of civilian police has 
been authorized, as well.</i>

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.560
<i>Well, "civilian police" is the media's name for it.</i>

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:51.090
<i>You mean the use of civilian companies, right?</i>

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:53.430
<i>With the Tokyo Summit coming up,</i>

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:55.520
<i>having more people is a big help.</i>

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.100
<i>Oh, I also heard that you know Governor Inagi.</i>

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.940
<i>Yeah, I've known him since we were kids.</i>

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.450
<i>He was such a wild child!</i>

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.430
Come on, now.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:06.750
<i>But his family home was lost</i>

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:13.110
<b>Tokyo Summit and Related Governmental Meetings 

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:13.110
<b>Tokyo Space Elevator 
Construction Plan</b>

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.200
<i>to the Quicksand Phenomenon.</i>

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.020
<i>Since the same thing happened to me, 
he looked out for me.</i>

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:13.110
<i>I see.</i>

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.650
What do you think is in 
store for Unit 8 after this?

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:19.070
Nothing important will change.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.810
We'll keep protecting you,

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.960
so keep supporting us!

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.850
<i>In the future,</i>

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:33.330
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:36.380
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.720
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:00.050
<b>File 1: The Man from the West</b>

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.010
<b>Unit 8</b>

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.900
Oh, yeah, it starts airing today!

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.480
Liko-chan, show me Asami-chan's commercial!

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:17.760
<i>Sure thing!</i>

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.910
<i>The one from the West Japan Office, right?</i>

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:20.510
Yeah.

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.440
<i>I'll look for it right now!</i>

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:26.170
I'd heard people talking, but I guess 
they really recorded it, huh?

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.850
It probably looks like the result of a lost bet.

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.450
She said it was a promotional video, but...

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:32.750
<i>Playing it now!</i>

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:38.130
<b>West Japan</b>

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.760
<i>When no one else is there,</i>

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.590
<i>you can count on Unit 9!</i>

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:48.430
<b>Unit 9</b>

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:48.430
<i>Leave West Japan to us!</i>

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:52.790
<i>Unit 9 is justice!</i>

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.510
<i>Please recommend us to your friends.</i>

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.440
Uh...

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.290
I heard Sena-san made a commercial, too?

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.070
Oh, the one from Nagoya, right?

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.890
<i>Here it is!</i>

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:08.570
<i>In Nagoya, where the golden 
shachihoko watches over us,</i>

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.660
<i>the Tanaka Tasuku Company</i>

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.440
<i>has been reborn as Senars, Inc.</i>

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.830
<i>For all your cleaning needs, 
from home to business,</i>

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.460
<i>come to Kodeki in Higashi Ward 
to find Senars, Inc.</i>

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.090
<i>Chinchikochin!</i>

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.590
Looks like they're having a good time.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.830
Quitting was probably the right call.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:29.810
Director Abigail...

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:31.050
What is it, boss?

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:34.520
Be sure to load things into the 
warehouse according to the rules I—

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.150
Don't sweat the small stuff, f**khead!

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:37.910
F**k—

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:42.520
Director, I respect that you've led this 
company since before I was born.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:46.420
But it would be a big help if you'd 
learn some more Japanese...

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.410
Boss, there are no f**king Japanese 
people here but you.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.620
No need for that crap.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.900
Okay... I get it.

00:05:55.790 --> 00:06:06.420
<b>Inbox 

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.800
What? That's rare.

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.050
<i>Hey, how are you?</i>

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:01.550
<i>We're about to get two new kids.</i>

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:04.470
<i>If they're anything like Baba Micchii, 
I'll send you a picture.</i>

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:08.550
<i>Oh, and I saw your CM and ha ha ha!</i>

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.550
Delete.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:11.300
Thanks for waiting, everyone!

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.800
Here are our new kids!

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:17.490
I am here as part of an exchange 
program with the Polska.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.810
I'm Emilia Edelman, and I shall do my best,

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:24.730
so please honor me with your instruction.

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:26.990
Your Japanese is very good.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:29.300
And the other...

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.150
Huh?

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.200
Hey, did you leave?

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:34.190
S-Sorry!

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.790
I'm here! Nice to meet you al!

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:39.250
Hey, no need to be so nervous.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.640
I-I'm sorry.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:43.290
I have scopophobia, so I just...

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:44.890
But I'll do my best.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:48.260
Oh, my name is Marimo. Kaburagi Marimo.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.460
Nice to meet you!

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:50.960
Will this work?

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:55.320
There are ways to deal with it, 
and Director Kaidou asked us to take her.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:56.060
Ma'am!

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:56.810
What?

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:58.470
A request for support!

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:02.430
There's an unknown Willwear user at an 
intersection near Takagi-cho, Shibuya!

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:03.230
<b>Shibuya Station</b>

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:04.700
They're ignoring orders to stop!

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.410
At this rate, maybe I'll be able to clear it.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:28.500
I hope Inagi-kun's worries are misplaced.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:29.420
What?

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:33.970
There's apparently a chance of indiscriminate 
terrorist attacks in the city.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:37.370
He was talking to foreign countries
in preparation for the summit,

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.060
and one of them shared that with him.

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:40.390
What's the agenda?

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:41.260
We don't know.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.710
Is it another issue with

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:46.280
increased migration and the accompanying 
discrimination and poverty?

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:50.280
It's a pain that they can't keep 
it within their own countries.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.440
<b>Requesting</b>

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:50.650
<b>Connection Approved</b>

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.020
Hey, Kaburagi, keep your eyes on the monitor.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.670
Uh, um...

00:07:57.670 --> 00:08:00.040
Marimo-chan, feel free to 
put on the data glasses.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:00.830
Okay!

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.220
I'm fine now.

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:04.240
The glasses fix it?

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:07.790
I-I'm sorry. The problem is fixed.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.260
Link the mobile assault command vehicle.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:14.340
Linking.

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:15.300
Linking.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:29.780
Tomorrow, between the hours of 9:00 and 14:00,

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:32.350
equip this and flee from the police.

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:34.500
Escape, and I'll give you ten million yen.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:36.160
What are you talking about?

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:39.520
This is a game played worldwide by celebrities.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:43.280
The whole thing will be broadcast by a 
series of fixed and security cameras.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.170
Viewers enjoy themselves by

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.930
placing massive bets on whether 
you can escape or not.

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:49.650
And if I can't?

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:53.340
I haven't worn a Willwear since 
training class in school.

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:56.020
Then you'll still get three million yen.

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:59.590
And we'll use our connections 
to have you released.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:02.630
That's way too good to be true.

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:05.040
It's up to you whether you believe it or not.

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.770
At this point, I'm going for the ten million.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:12.570
<b>Shibuya Station</b>

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:15.750
Is the suspect's Willwear planning 
to go toward Yoyogi?

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:17.840
It was heading to Daikanyama.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.950
What do you think their goal is?

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.200
Haruka-chan, get ready.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.770
We'll launch from Komaba.

00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:23.330
Okay!

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.250
<b>Normal Car          Command Car</b>

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:31.000
Vitals, all green.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.000
Lock!

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.720
I-Inner unit, begin output.

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:44.990
Oscar III, set Metistructure Ibuki Unit.

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:06.070
Data-link complete.

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:07.500
Request permission to launch.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:08.750
Permission granted.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:09.750
Permission granted.

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:10.750
Launching!

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.680
Oh, crap! Unit 8!

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.130
This is the police.

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:26.100
Move to the side of the road and shut 
down your Willwear immediately.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:26.980
You have—

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:30.220
Command vehicle, this is Oscar III.

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:32.750
May I use Shibuya's internal systems?

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:33.770
Permission granted.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:34.690
Permission confirmed.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.690
<b>Shibuya Station</b>

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:39.040
Hit!

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.030
Suspect's current location found.

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:43.030
I'll send the Willwear data, too.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:46.440
Huh? Now it's heading to Harajuku.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:49.080
These parts... It can't be...

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:52.470
Shall I use my Mjölnir to destroy 
the target's battery?

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.790
Good idea. Smash it—

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:55.300
Wait!

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:58.130
Don't hit it with a shock that strong!

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:00.180
Its equipment setup is

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.970
the same one used by African suicide bombers!

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:04.550
Suicide bombers?

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:07.830
The battery pack is covered with explosives.

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:12.400
And when it blows, the rest 
of the armor explodes, too.

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.550
A bullet from a gun isn't enough to detonate it,

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:18.460
but it's not enough to 
destroy the battery, either.

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:18.990
Meaning...

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:21.950
It's waiting for us to attack it?

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.770
Then why did it run away?

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:25.390
Well, that's a good point...

00:11:25.390 --> 00:11:27.900
Oh, I just got an ID on the suspect.

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.600
Looks like a teenage girl.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:33.070
A report from sector 4 says a security camera

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:37.380
spotted her at the old city hall's demolition site.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:39.000
Haraguchi Yuria.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.050
They learned the contents of her 
conversation by reading her lips.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:45.180
If she can successfully flee until 14:00, 
and then reach Tokyo Station,

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:46.350
she'll get ten million yen.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:50.770
Does this mean that if we do nothing, 
the Willwear will explode at 14:00?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.060
Yes, that's correct.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.990
I see. Understood.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:56.470
We have no choice.

00:11:56.780 --> 00:11:58.910
I'm designating everything within

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:01.730
a one-kilometer radius of that 
mobile Willwear an alert zone.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:02.800
Understood.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:05.200
That will have a major effect.

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:09.140
But our first priority is citizen safety.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:13.510
Oscar III, head back. We'll devise a new plan.

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:14.370
Understood.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:17.120
According to the data in the 
association's libraries,

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.380
the only possibility is this point.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.820
If we shoot at this angle, we can destroy 
the battery's control circuits.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:24.810
Isn't that point too small?

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:26.590
Taking into account temperature and humidity...

00:12:26.590 --> 00:12:28.390
We'll need a sniper.

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:31.390
Do we have any who can use a Willwear?

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.140
Boss, I'll go after all.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:34.640
Capture her and there's no problem.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:38.810
But if someone is watching her, 
they might detonate right then!

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.400
Almost got my ten million!

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:45.380
Good work, everyone.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:48.500
We'll now separate the trash we've gathered.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:49.800
Follow the rules and—

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.230
Hurry, you c*****kers!

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:51.870
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:59.740
Yes, this is Senars, Inc., 
where we're always clean.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:02.330
Sena-kun, it's me, Yamabuki!

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.480
It's been so long. How have you been?

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:08.140
Well, I'm in a bind because I don't have a sniper.

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:11.570
Huh?

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:18.240
I see... A suicide bomber.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:20.700
I understand the situation, but...

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:24.030
I want you to help us. We need your talent.

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:26.910
But I'm part of a civilian company now.

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:31.890
Didn't you hear that they adjusted the 
terrorism laws at the last Diet meeting

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:34.600
to allow more civilian cooperation?

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:35.500
Sorry.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:38.420
All I've read lately is the <i>Garbage Man's Times</i>.

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:42.420
Um... Well, a lot happened, so it's okay now.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:45.110
We already have a helicopter 
en route with the unit.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.930
But how does that work with the rules?

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:49.800
From Unit 8?

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:50.590
Yes.

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:52.810
They want immediate permission from Tokyo.

00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:54.390
What shall we do?

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:58.230
This will be the first case of civilian 
cooperation in the entire country.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:13:59.210
I'll give permission.

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:01.360
I promised their section chief

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.980
I'd make things easier for them.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.020
It's okay, really!

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:10.430
But it's been so long since I left the front lines...

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:13.270
Enough of this, boss!

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:15.530
Talking with that dimwit is a waste of time.

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:16.450
I'll start up my Willwear—

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:17.870
Shut up for a second!

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:20.150
Sena-kun, the law says it's okay, and I have

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:22.000
permission from the relevant authorities.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:22.790
And the money—

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.460
Money isn't the issue.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.870
I'm worried about the lack of practice, I guess.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:30.390
Boss, no problem.

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:33.590
You look super good in your police photos.

00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:35.900
Do it, let's do it. No problem.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:37.730
Director Abigail,

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:41.020
I don't remember ever showing you a photo.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.780
So what, you wa**er?!

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:47.110
Pay's good, company's hurting, can't pay salaries!

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:48.740
Have no money, di****ad!

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:53.600
I understand, Section Chief Yamabuki.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:54.700
I'll do it.

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:55.750
Thank you!

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:58.540
Ask the person picking you up for the details.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.340
Sena-san! It's been forever!

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:08.850
Hey, Haruka-kun.

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:11.470
I've never seen this before. Is it Unit 8's?

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:14.410
We're spending more time away from base.

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:16.410
You can equip your Willwear here,

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:18.810
and even data-link to the command vehicle.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:21.580
Wow, Unit 8's hit the big time.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:22.730
Boss!

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:23.740
Yes?

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:26.860
You look good. Gonna give up the company?

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.310
Don't worry.

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:30.650
This is the job I was born to do.

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:34.910
I left law enforcement to make a career change, 
and I found the job I was made for.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:37.670
An old man joke!

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:36.660
<b>Made a career change (<i>tenshoku</i>)</b>

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.450
<b>Made a career change (<i>tenshoku</i>) 

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:38.870
It's not.

00:15:40.310 --> 00:15:43.160
You! Move to the side of the road, 
and shut down that Willwear!

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.710
Do you know what you're doing?

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:45.640
What's going on?

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:47.810
The police stopped doing anything.

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:49.380
Well, that's fine.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.350
I just have to make it to the goal.

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:53.140
This Willwear has

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:56.250
its external microphones disabled.

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:58.390
<b>Kanda Station 

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:58.390
<b>Projected Route</b>

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:59.080
Ninety minutes remain until 
her goal at Tokyo Station.

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:03.100
Our missing member, Oscar I, 
will just make it here in time.

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:07.200
If Sena-san fails, it will explode, right?

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:07.900
Yes.

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:10.320
But we'll cross that bridge when we get to it.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:13.250
Is it all right to ask a civilian 
to take such a risk?

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:14.570
He was originally one of us.

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:18.880
I sent Sena-kun's data to 
both you and Marimo-chan.

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:19.740
Take a look.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:21.700
O-Okay, I'll have a look.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:27.380
H-He's super elite!

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:29.440
He attended the National 
Defense Academy of Japan!

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:31.340
Why would someone as amazing as this...

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:35.330
Officially, he's a guy who 
really has his act together,

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:37.490
but he's not the type to get attached.

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:40.810
When his private life gets messed up, 
he'll give up on anything.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:43.450
I hope he's gotten a little better.

00:16:45.740 --> 00:16:48.700
Vitals, all green. Lock.

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:01.100
Oscar I, set Elf Sigma Unit.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.040
<b>Sena Souichirou</b>

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.040
You kept this for me.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:07.130
It's customized for you, 
so we all decided to keep it.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:08.510
The codename, too?

00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:10.260
That's right, Oscar I.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:12.840
Oscar I... That brings back memories.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:16.020
All right. I'll do my best.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.270
Now, the question is if things happen 
how Inspector Kuroki expects.

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:24.390
His intuition's sharp at times like these.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.690
Inner unit, begin output.

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:33.430
Oscar II, set strike interceptor unit.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:42.290
Governor, Unit 8 says they're almost 
ready to begin their attack.

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:43.560
Got it.

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:45.690
How goes the evacuation around Tokyo Station?

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:46.910
It's complete.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:50.420
What's that?

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:52.430
This is Oscar I.

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:54.420
Temperature and humidity are fine.

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:55.800
I'll aim from here.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.880
Roger. Ten minutes until the limit.

00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:59.330
All authorities have given approval.

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:00.010
Then I'll—

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:01.570
Oscar I!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.680
I knew there'd be an observer!

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:06.050
Oscar II?

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:08.520
Your field of vision is always so narrow, Oscar I!

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:12.090
That just means we have different roles.

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:14.340
Yeah?

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:16.360
Then I'll fight

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:17.330
this guy!

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:26.330
This looks bad. I'll make for the goal.

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:30.060
The target...

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:30.880
Haruka-kun!

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:33.630
Roger. We'll head for Tokyo Station 
and ambush her there.

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:38.850
How could you trick a minor 
into being a suicide bomber?

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:46.100
You bastard!

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.310
Oscar II, forget him and support Oscar I!

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:51.580
Command vehicle, this is Oscar I.

00:18:51.580 --> 00:18:52.650
We're in position.

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:54.650
We'll do one final check.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:56.700
Is it set to use small-caliber ammunition?

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.610
Yes, ammo's .22.

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:00.690
Then fire whenever.

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:03.650
<i>She's moving around so much.</i>

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:07.340
<i>And if I miss, the person in the Willwear...</i>

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:13.540
I-It's no good, Section Chief.

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:14.510
I can't do it.

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:15.940
Too late for that now!

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:18.270
What are you waiting for, dimwit?

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:21.220
You can't do anything alone, can you?

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:24.140
What did you say, you lazy-ass public servant?

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:26.110
Do you know how hard it is,

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:29.870
getting along with city hall and tracking 
hours, welfare payments, and work visas?

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:31.330
I do not!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:34.960
You're the one who wanted to leave, 
so don't come back and lecture me!

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.110
Quiet, you careless fool!

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:43.920
We did it! It worked!

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:45.700
We stopped the explosion!

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.090
Huh? The battery's out of power?

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:51.820
You can do it if you try, so just do it!

00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:54.070
Right. Thanks to you, I could concentrate.

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:55.120
Thank you.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.920
In case you missed it, that was sarcasm.

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:58.310
Right, right.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:01.590
Oh, no... Boss, the criminal...

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:09.390
Which personality is Kaburagi-san's default?

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:10.520
I don't know.

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:14.080
Um, if you're worried about the 
inner, then Haruka-san...

00:20:16.850 --> 00:20:19.910
Man, I was so close to winning ten million yen!

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:22.030
Your life isn't worth much, is it?

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:23.530
Did you say something?

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:27.490
You were almost used in a suicide attack.

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:36.920
No, it was fun to see you guys after so long.

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.520
And you new kids, too. Work hard.

00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:40.280
Okay!

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:43.080
Why don't you just stay here?

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:45.510
You're our first civilian cooperator.

00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:49.470
My company's just getting off the ground.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:51.500
Aw, don't be like that...

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:52.040
Oh, thank you. That's a big help.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:53.460
Goodbye, then.

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:55.190
CEO Sena.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:55.830
Yes?

00:20:56.130 --> 00:21:00.130
You're going to be staying here 
as part of a transfer.

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:01.150
Huh?

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.690
Since you're guaranteed payment,

00:21:03.690 --> 00:21:06.050
we'll be keeping you for a little while.

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:09.620
Your director says she'll kick 
your ass if you go back.

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:11.880
She'd do it, too.

00:21:12.220 --> 00:21:14.210
I guess I don't have a choice. Understood.

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:17.960
So you're our new civilian cooperator.

00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:19.540
Make your introduction!

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:20.700
Right.

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:22.510
I'm Sena Souichirou, a new team member.

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:25.510
I'm sure I'll have a lot to learn,

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:28.680
but I look forward to working with all of you.

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:37.800
I'll tell it to you straight. I don't like you.

00:21:37.800 --> 00:21:40.770
Thanks. I hate you, too.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:41.400
But...

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:44.840
Yeah. If you're coming back, I want your help.

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:47.610
More weird crimes are happening again.

00:21:48.560 --> 00:21:51.900
Do they have something to do with 
the upcoming Tokyo Summit?

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:53.780
I don't know.

00:21:53.780 --> 00:21:56.070
But there's more terrorism like today's.

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:59.080
Come to think of it, what happened 
to the observer Willwear?

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:01.170
They're looking for it, but it won't be easy.

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:03.210
Where's Mythos now?

00:22:03.650 --> 00:22:04.700
That is

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:07.050
top-secret.

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:09.190
I see.

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:13.100
Later. Work starts tomorrow.

00:22:13.640 --> 00:22:14.710
And...

00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:18.200
Kyoukai-san said he'd repaint your Willwear.

00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:19.510
It's gonna be shocking pink.

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.360
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:51.190 --> 00:23:53.330
Ohakonyapachininko! It's Liko!

00:23:52.360 --> 00:24:04.910
File 2: Endless Avenger

00:23:53.330 --> 00:23:54.740
Just kidding, it's Rin!

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:56.970
Why are you pretending to be cute, boss?

00:23:56.970 --> 00:23:58.650
Huh? Pretending?

00:23:58.650 --> 00:23:59.570
Sorry!

00:23:59.570 --> 00:24:03.240
Okay, I'll use my curse's power to 
put you in danger next time!

00:24:03.240 --> 00:24:04.330
Oh, no!
